      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Saint Xavier University Career Pages For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Center of Health and Wellness Personal Trainer Graduate Assistant - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Center of Health and Wellness Personal Trainer Graduate Assistant - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Employment Opportunities Menu Employment Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Saint Xavier University Career Pages powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Center of Health and Wellness Personal Trainer Graduate Assistant - Student Employment Print Apply ﻿ Center of Health and Wellness Personal Trainer Graduate Assistant - Student Employment Salary $20.00 Hourly Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Student Employment - FWS Required Job Number 01541 Department SONHS - Center for Health & Wellness - SE Opening Date 08/04/2026 Summary The graduate assistant (GA) for the Center of Health and Wellness (CHW) will work with clients on a one-to-one basis or in small groups to support their health journey. The personal trainer is responsible for setting times, adhering to the schedule for working with their clients and ensuring that CHW rules and regulations are followed. This student employment opportunity supports the development of skills aligned with the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies . Through this role, students will strengthen the following competencies: Communication: Students build communication skills by practicing clear, respectful, and professional verbal, written, and interpersonal communication in a workplace setting. Critical Thinking: Students build critical thinking skills by applying judgment, solving problems, prioritizing tasks, maintaining accuracy, and using feedback to improve their work. Professionalism: Students build professionalism by practicing dependability, accountability, confidentiality when applicable, workplace etiquette, and respectful service in a workplace setting. Teamwork: Students build teamwork skills by collaborating with supervisors, staff, and peers to support department goals, assist others, and contribute to a positive work environment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities The position will fulfill the commitment of the role titled, Personal trainer. This role will provide the following: Health assessments in accordance with the CHW policy manual One on one personal training Small group training sessions Cleaning the weight room and center Scheduling clients Ensuring all forms are correctly filled out Presentations to the community on health and wellness Qualifications MUST BE A STUDENT AT SAINT XAVIER UNIVERSITY Must be Federal Work Study E ligible Must Include a Resume and Cover Letter Bachelor’s degree is required and full-time enrollment in a graduate program must meet eligibility requirements for admission to Graduate Studies at Saint Xavier University National certification preferred Undergrad in exercise science or related field of study Previous coaching experience preferred Ability to demonstrate and teach Olympic lifts, running mechanics and change of direction mechanics The candidate will possess a good work ethic, attention to detail, ability to manage sensitive and confidential student information and a familiarity with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) Proficiency in social media is preferred Strong communication skills are preferred Upholds and supports the mission of Saint Xavier University Description of Hours: 10 hours per week will be the time commitment to the Division of Health Sciences Center for Health and Wellness. Students who are GA’s will be paid through the Federal Work Study program at an hourly rate. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n   