ole, students will strengthen the following competencies: Communication: Students build communication skills by practicing clear, respectful, and professional verbal, written, and interpersonal communication in a workplace setting. Leadership: Students build leadership skills by taking initiative, demonstrating responsibility, supporting others, contributing ideas, and modeling positive workplace behaviors. Professionalism: Students build professionalism by practicing dependability, accountability, confidentiality when applicable, workplace etiquette, and respectful service in a workplace setting. Teamwork: Students build teamwork skills by collaborating with supervisors, staff, and peers to support department goals, assist others, and contribute to a positive work environment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities LA’s are expected to attend class as designated by the instructor of the course. LA’s are expected to assist students with various academic skills and course content. LA’s answer questions, facilitate discussion, and assist the instructor of the course. Additional administrative responsibilities, as assigned. Qualifications MUST BE A STUDENT AT SAINT XAVIER UNIVERSITY Must Include a Resume and Cover Letter Federal Work Study is NOT a requirement. Students who are Federal Work Study eligible may still apply for this position. Must be enrolled as a SXU student Must have an A in computer science class in which you want to tutor Must be able to complete all staff development responsibilities Must exhibit appropriate and professional behavior at all times Must be friendly and enjoy working with people Description of Hours: Up to 5 hours per week Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my p