      "title": "Chemistry Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Saint Xavier University Career Pages For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Chemistry Lab Assistant - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Chemistry Lab Assistant - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Employment Opportunities Menu Employment Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Saint Xavier University Career Pages powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Chemistry Lab Assistant - Student Employment Print Apply ﻿ Chemistry Lab Assistant - Student Employment Salary $17.05 Hourly Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Student Employment - FWS Required Job Number 01644 Department Chemistry SE Opening Date 09/01/2026 Summary The Chemistry Lab Assistant works with the Chemistry faculty and Laboratory Coordinators and learns to handle the logistics, preparation, and safety of instructional laboratories. This role is vital for ensuring that undergraduate chemistry experiments run efficiently, safely, and cleanly. It provides an excellent hands-on opportunity for students to gain practical laboratory experience, reinforce their chemistry knowledge, and learn industry-standard chemical hygiene practices. This student employment opportunity supports the development of skills aligned with the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies. Through this role, students will strengthen the following competencies: Communication: Students build communication skills by practicing clear, respectful, and professional verbal, written, and interpersonal communication in a workplace setting. Critical Thinking: Students build critical thinking skills by applying judgment, solving problems, prioritizing tasks, maintaining accuracy, and using feedback to improve their work. Teamwork: Students build teamwork skills by collaborating with supervisors, staff, and peers to support department goals, assist others, and contribute to a positive work environment. Technology: Students build technology skills by using department systems, software, digital tools, equipment, or university platforms to complete tasks accurately and efficiently. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Lab Preparation & Setup Accurately measures, weighs, and mix chemicals to prepare stock solutions and reagents for scheduled experiments. Set up of laboratory apparatus, glassware, and analytical instruments before classes begin. Aliquot and distribute chemicals into proper, clearly labeled containers at student benches. Read and review course lab manuals and prep sheets ahead of time to verify inventory needs. Maintenance & Organization Clean and restock laboratory glassware and equipment after student use. Maintain the overall cleanliness and order of the chemistry stockroom, chemical storage areas, and main student laboratories. Clean and calibrate laboratory balances and ensure balances remain chemical-free. Monitor inventory of consumable supplies, reporting shortages to the Lab Coordinator Safety & Chemical Hygiene Strictly abide by institutional safety procedures and policies outlined in the Chemical Hygiene Plan. Assist with the proper collection, labeling, and temporary storage of chemical waste. Safely handle gas cylinders, empty glass waste bins, and maintain safety equipment stations. Identify and immediately report broken glassware or malfunctioning hardware to the Lab Coordinator. Instructional Support Help guide students in the correct, safe setup of their laboratory equipment during active sessions. Help faculty locate supplies and restock reagents mid-session when needed. Qualifications MUST BE A STUDENT AT SAINT XAVIER UNIVERSITY Must be Federal Work Study E ligible Must Include a Resume and Cover Letter Major or Minor in Chemistry. Responsibilities increase with developing abilities Description of Hours: 10hrs/week Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Poli