      "title": "Graduate Assistant for CSDI 202: Prof. Writing",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Saint Xavier University Career Pages For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Graduate Assistant for CSDI 202: Prof. Writing - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Graduate Assistant for CSDI 202: Prof. Writing - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Employment Opportunities Menu Employment Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Saint Xavier University Career Pages powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Graduate Assistant for CSDI 202: Prof. Writing - Student Employment Print Apply ﻿ Graduate Assistant for CSDI 202: Prof. Writing - Student Employment Salary $20.00 Hourly Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Student Employment - FWS Required Job Number 01621 Department SONHS - Communication Sciences & Disorders SE (correct) Opening Date 08/11/2026 Summary Teaching assistants (TA) in CSD at Saint Xavier will have the opportunity to participate in a wide range of activities tailored to the course assignment. As a TA, the student will gain practical experience in supporting classroom instruction, facilitating student learning, and assisting with course administration. The emphasis will be placed on developing pedagogical skills, understanding diverse learning needs, and fostering an inclusive educational environment. This is ideal for students aspiring to hold future roles as educators, researchers, or clinical supervisors in academia or educational settings within the field of communication disorders. This student employment opportunity supports the development of skills aligned with the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies. Through this role, students will strengthen the following competencies: Communication: Students build communication skills by practicing clear, respectful, and professional verbal, written, and interpersonal communication in a workplace setting. Critical Thinking: Students build critical thinking skills by applying judgment, solving problems, prioritizing tasks, maintaining accuracy, and using feedback to improve their work. Professionalism: Students build professionalism by practicing dependability, accountability, confidentiality when applicable, workplace etiquette, and respectful service in a workplace setting. Technology: Students build technology skills by using department systems, software, digital tools, equipment, or university platforms to complete tasks accurately and efficiently. Essential Duties & Responsibilities TAs are responsible for assisting faculty with teaching and administrative tasks, including but not limited to: Assisting faculty with classroom instruction, records, and assignments Leading discussion sections (if TA is available during class) Meeting with students during TA Student Support Hours/Review Sessions (plan for 1 hr /week) Leading student reviews before each quiz Assist with grading quizzes (answer key provided) Assist with grading projects Preparing in-class activity materials Recording and calculating grades Providing feedback on assignments Proctoring examinations Taking attendance or monitoring participation Prepare and distribute course materials (if the TA is available during class) Meeting with faculty 1x/week Completing administrative tasks (e.g., photocopying, printing) Identify evidence-based resources that can support course content Communicate student concerns/needs with faculty Qualifications MUST BE A STUDENT AT SAINT XAVIER UNIVERSITY Must be Federal Work Study E ligible Must Include a Resume and Cover Letter The Graduate Assistant will provide writing support to students across the CSD curriculum, with a focus on professional and clinical writing. Responsibilities include grading assignments, providing structured feedback on written work, supporting APA formatting, and holding writing focused office hours. This role may also serve as a general writing resource for students in other CSD courses. Strong writing skills are required. Hours: 10 hours per week Supervisor: Kristina Simak Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updatin