      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Saint Xavier University Career Pages For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Open Rank- English Department Chair | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Open Rank- English Department Chair | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Employment Opportunities Menu Employment Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Saint Xavier University Career Pages powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Open Rank- English Department Chair Print Apply ﻿ Open Rank- English Department Chair Salary $67,000.00 - $72,000.00 Annually Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 01452 Department Language & Literature Opening Date 04/01/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Department of Language and Literature, housed within the College of Liberal Arts & Education at Saint Xavier University, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track open rank department chair faculty position in English with expertise in writing and rhetoric. The Department of Language and Literature supports the General Education two course writing requirement, Middle Level and Secondary Education English Language Arts majors, Spanish in the Professions major, Spanish PK-12 Education major, and various minors. Critical aspects of the position will be to support the development and assessment of highly effective general education writing courses, to develop, review, and assess the English and Spanish teacher preparation majors (middle and secondary English education, and Spanish PK-12 education) in alignment with Illinois State Board of Education requirements in collaboration with the Education Division, and to develop, review, and assess the Spanish in the Professions major. The position has a start date in the Fall of 2026 and entails a ten-month contract which includes nine months during the academic year and one month over the summer. Rank depends on credentials and years of experience. Saint Xaiver University was founded by the Sisters of Mercy in 1846 and is guided by fundamental values of the Sisters to serve the underserved. Saint Xavier University is a Hispanic Serving Institution, serves a significant percentage of minority and first-generation college students, and is recognized as a top performer on social mobility and one of the most diverse student populations among regional universities in the Midwest by U.S. News & World Report . Essential Duties & Responsibilities Teach 9 credit hours each semester of English courses related to one’s area of expertise Lead all activities of the Department of Language and Literature Manage the curriculum and assessment for the majors, minors, and general education course offerings Hire, supervise, evaluate, mentor, and support adjunct and full-time faculty Establish a program of research leading to peer-reviewed publications and presentations Provide service to the program, college, and university Qualifications Doctorate in English, Composition and Rhetoric, or closely related field Excellence in collegiate teaching grounded in evidence-based best practices for teaching and learning, particularly in writing Experience with curriculum design and assessment Experience with or potential for excellence in leadership Evidence of potential for peer-reviewed scholarship COMPENSATION Salary and rank will be determined by credentials and experience. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS Please provide a cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, research narrative or philosophy, leadership experience or philosophy, sample syllabus for an undergraduate writing course, copies of transcripts for all degrees (unofficial copies acceptable), and contact information for three letters of recommendation. References will be contacted at a later date for finalists only. Please name files as “Lastname_CV,” etc. Questions about the position can be directed to Dr. Angela Pirlott, Dean, College of Liberal Arts & Education and Search Committee Chair, at pirlott@sxu.edu . DEADLINE Review of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Saint Xavier University is committed to providing employees with a comprehensive benefits package that meets the needs of both the individual and his/her family.  Many of the benefits are flexible and offer choices to meet various benefit needs.  SXU employment benefits can be found here . Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standa