Employment - FWS Exempt Job Number 01615 Department Center for Learning & Student Support SE Opening Date 08/11/2026 Summary CLASS peer subject tutors work one-on-one or in small groups with students for a broad range of academic disciplines. This student employment opportunity supports the development of skills aligned with the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies. Through this role, students will strengthen the following competencies: Communication: Students build communication skills by practicing clear, respectful, and professional verbal, written, and interpersonal communication in a workplace setting. Critical Thinking: Students build critical thinking skills by applying judgment, solving problems, prioritizing tasks, maintaining accuracy, and using feedback to improve their work. Professionalism: Students build professionalism by practicing dependability, accountability, confidentiality when applicable, workplace etiquette, and respectful service in a workplace setting. Teamwork: Students build teamwork skills by collaborating with supervisors, staff, and peers to support department goals, assist others, and contribute to a positive work environment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities The following identifies the primary and essential functions of the position and is not intended to be an exhaustive listing of all duties. Subject-specific tutors help students understand course content and teach them about relevant academic skills necessary for success in the course. Upon request and direction of the CLASS executive director and project coordinator, tutors may work with professors to provide special tutoring assistance and to promote services in classes. Tutors are responsible for maintaining accurate appointment records and completing written reports of each session in Navigate Tutors must participate in mandatory training meetings and ongoing professional development, equivalent to 10 hours each semester. Tutors complete other tasks or projects as assigned by the supervisor. Maintain the confidentiality of our clients and services. Exhibit appropriate and professional behavior. Are responsible, dependable and punctual in their duties, in the completion of assigned tasks, and in notifying the appropriate staff personnel when conflicts or problems occur. Qualifications MUST BE A STUDENT AT SAINT XAVIER UNIVERSITY Must Include a Resume and Cover Letter Federal Work Study is NOT a requirement. Students who are Federal Work Study eligible may still apply for this position. CLASS Peer Subject Tutor Qualifications To be considered for employment as a CLASS peer subject tutor, students must: Demonstrate significant knowledge in the subject matter and advanced communications skills, typically confirmed by two professors. Be a current Saint Xavier University student, with a 3.0 GPA, and complete the course(s) in which he/she wishes to tutor earning a B or better.   (A grade of “A” is preferred). Possess analytical and advanced communication skills to evaluate and articulate suggestions for peers’ improvement. Be able to work with their peers in a manner that is encouraging, and which fosters confidence and enthusiasm to increase knowledge of the subject matter. Be able to work independently and to take initiative in fulfilling their responsibilities. Exhibit excellent interpersonal skills and ease in relating to people from varying educational, cultural, and social backgrounds with various levels of skills and abilities. Description of Hours: · Up to 10 hours per week Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to al