afety Opening Date 09/03/2026 Summary The Dispatcher directs public safety police, security and emergency medical personnel regarding calls for service, and answers and notifies proper emergency personnel when utilizing the campus 911 system. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Monitors emergency switchboard alarms and E911 on-site notification system. Monitors University emergency 3-911 phone and directs Public Safety personnel as necessary. Primary fielder and router of calls to Department of Public Safety. Monitors the Public Safety radio system and are responsible for logging calls for service on shift activity log. Serves as an emergency command post when need arise. Attend internal and/or external training courses, classes, and seminars to further develop public safety dispatching skills and knowledge. Maintain the strictest confidentiality of all information or situations that are gathered or are made aware of during the course of your duties. Maintain regular communication with officers and supervisory personnel and communicate of situations occurring on campus. Maintain a constant presence at the dispatch center. Responsible for contacting the Public Safety supervisor on duty, Resident Assistants on duty, and the on-call Resident Director in case of emergency. Have a duty to call local Emergency response services at the request of an on-duty supervisor and facilitate their assistance on campus if necessary. Become knowledgeable of all Public Safety and University policies and procedures. Maintain a courteous and pleasant environment and a well-groomed appearance. Be prepared to function accordingly based upon the needs of the department. Monitor access control system, security camera systems and emergency phones and advise supervisors when maintenance is required. Perform other related duties as requested. Qualifications To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities who are otherwise qualified to perform the essential functions. High school diploma or GED Must be 21 years of age or older Must maintain a valid driver's license with a record acceptable to our insurance carrier Must pass a background check that includes submitting fingerprints to the Illinois State Police and FBI. Must pass and maintain Illinois LEADS certification. Cannot have any felony convictions, or have been convicted of domestic violence or related crimes. Extensive and excellence interpersonal skills, the ability to effectively communicate, and solve problems. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this s