rly Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Student Employment - FWS Required Job Number 01593 Department Student Media SE Opening Date 08/12/2026 Summary The Videographer is in charge of the entire library of photo/image/video content that will be published by the Department of Student Media, both online and internally. She/he will attend official SXU events to take pictures, shoot video, and maintain the archive of The Department of Student Media. This student employment opportunity supports the development of skills aligned with the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies. Through this role, students will strengthen the following competencies: Professionalism: Students build professionalism by practicing dependability, accountability, confidentiality when applicable, workplace etiquette, and respectful service in a workplace setting. Teamwork: Students build teamwork skills by collaborating with supervisors, staff, and peers to support department goals, assist others, and contribute to a positive work environment. Technology: Students build technology skills by using department systems, software, digital tools, equipment, or university platforms to complete tasks accurately and efficiently. Communication: Students build communication skills by practicing clear, respectful, and professional verbal, written, and interpersonal communication in a workplace setting. Essential Duties & Responsibilities In charge of all picture content for Student Media including: The Xavierite and WXAV 88.3FM Attends SXU events to supply pictures for publication in The Xavierite. Collaborates with student djs and writers in shooting interviews with potential guests Publishes video and photography across Student Media’s various social media platforms Leading member of the Entertainment Committee. Has experience utilizing the Adobe Cloud Suite, specifically: Photoshop, Premier, InDesign, and Illustrator. Attend weekly general staff 