      "title": "Vocational Specialist",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Saint Xavier University Career Pages For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Vocational Specialist  | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Vocational Specialist  | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Employment Opportunities Menu Employment Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Saint Xavier University Career Pages powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Vocational Specialist Print Apply ﻿ Vocational Specialist Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Adjunct Faculty Job Number 01614 Department SONHS - Communication Sciences & Disorders Opening Date 08/18/2026 Per Credit Hour $1,080.00 Summary The Vocational Specialist manages the Community of Adult Cougars Helping (C.O.A.C.H.) specialty clinic operations and provides administrative support to the faculty and graduate students within the Communication Sciences & Disorders Program. This individual supports Ludden Speech & Language Clients with disabilities and communication barriers with the goal of building skills, workplace relationship, and independence leading to employment. Manages multiple responsibilities while interacting with clients, students and faculty in a busy academic and clinic environment. This is a grant funded position. Monday 8:30 – 12:30, fall semester 2026 Essential Duties & Responsibilities 1. Create connections and secure sites for the placement of adult clients with disabilities to provide a clinical site for SXU SLP students to gain clinical experience while adult clients develop communication skills required for employment. 2. Share success stories and act as an advisor for other interested employers. 3. Create an intake process for the functional assessment of clients who apply to the program for admission. 4. Develop and maintain vocational training curriculum. 5. Coach, encourage and support individuals on and off the job sites to help them build professionalism, interpersonal skills and gain independence. 6. Provide one-on-one, hands-on instruction at the job site to help the individual learn specific tasks and meet employer expectations. 7. Help clients navigate social dynamics, advocate for necessary accommodations, and communicate effectively with supervisors. 8. Investigate the feasibility of support for parent guidance on finding employment for adult children. 9. Encourage problem solving to work through issues that arise. 10. Provide positive feedback and areas for improvement related to the individual’s performance and employer expectations. 11. Create and update records and reports on progress. 12. Coordinate and monitor transportation as this can be a barrier to site placement. 13. Coordinate team building events and activities as appropriate. 14. Complete all other duties or assigned as needed. Qualifications College degree in social work required. Three or more years of related experience working with adults with disabilities in a school or clinic setting. Knowledge of Illinois programs of adults with disabilities. Exceptional communication skills (oral and written), organizational, interpersonal and time management skills. Attention to detail and ability to multi-task, meet deadlines, work independently, and prioritize. Ability to work with a diverse population in a professional, courteous, and tactful manner. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. Saint Xavier University affirms its position as a Catholic institution, inspired by the heritage of the Sisters of Mercy, and asserts its rights to employ persons who subscribe to the mission, vision and core values of the University. Saint Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer that makes all decisions regarding recruitment, hiring, promotions and all other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the grounds of race, color, creed, sex, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status or other factors protected by law. Hiring decisions will be based on the bona fide occupational qualifications of each applicant. Employer Saint Xavier University Address 3700 West 103rd Street Chicago, Illinois, 60655 Phone 773-298-3452 Website http://www.sxu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Employment Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Cli