      "title": "WXAV Music Director",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Saint Xavier University Career Pages For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser WXAV Music Director - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. WXAV Music Director - Student Employment | Saint Xavier University Career Pages page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Employment Opportunities Menu Employment Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Saint Xavier University Career Pages powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" WXAV Music Director - Student Employment Print Apply ﻿ WXAV Music Director - Student Employment Salary $17.05 Hourly Location 3700 W. 103rd Street, Chicago, IL Job Type Student Employment - FWS Required Job Number 01600 Department Student Media SE Opening Date 08/12/2026 Summary The WXAV Music Director works with record companies to keep the station well supplied with the latest releases; listens to all new music to check and edit lyrics for compliance with FCC and WXAV rules and regulations for broadcast. This student employment opportunity supports the development of skills aligned with the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies. Through this role, students will strengthen the following competencies: Communication: Students build communication skills by practicing clear, respectful, and professional verbal, written, and interpersonal communication in a workplace setting. Professionalism: Students build professionalism by practicing dependability, accountability, confidentiality when applicable, workplace etiquette, and respectful service in a workplace setting. Teamwork: Students build teamwork skills by collaborating with supervisors, staff, and peers to support department goals, assist others, and contribute to a positive work environment. Technology: Students build technology skills by using department systems, software, digital tools, equipment, or university platforms to complete tasks accurately and efficiently. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Publishes a weekly NACC chart for industry publication and record companies to see what new music WXAV is playing. The Music Director co-ordinates and oversees the WXAV music committee to decide what new music the station will be playing and maintains the music library- both digital (computer) and physical (CDs). The Music Director arranges interviews and station giveaways for the WXAV staff to participate in. Along with the other members of management, the music director evaluates various student broadcasts, to ensure that FCC rules and regulations are met, and to offer feedback on the DJ’s program. The Music Director also assists in planning, and promoting of promotional events. Qualifications MUST BE A STUDENT AT SAINT XAVIER UNIVERSITY Must be Federal Work Study E ligible Must Include a Resume and Cover Letter Background in Communication preferred. Additional Expectations We inspire success by working together to provide meaningful, personalized service in a spirit of excellence. SXU seeks candidates that deliver value-added services in a responsive, collaborative, effective, and respectful manner. The University is committed to diversity and encourages applications from individuals with a wide variety of bac